Z||000000||Two88GTs||03-25-2001||06:59 AM||||Greetings!  This is my first post and I hope someone can help me.  The horn stopped working on one of my 88GTs this past week.  I traced it back to a blown fuse(#8 in the fusebox, 20 amps).<BR>When I replaced the fuse and press the horn button, the fuse immediately blows again.  I'm guessing that maybe the ground wire for the horn has gone south?  I'm almost embarrassed to ask this, but where is the horn located in a Fiero?  Also, is it possible to change the belts without jacking up the car and removing the inner RR fender?<BR>Thank you in advance.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Wolfhound||03-25-2001||08:07 AM||||There are actually two horns,behind the facia on both sides. A high and low tone I guess you'd call it. You can access them by detaching the flexable shields from underneath.<BR>The 87 serpentine belt can be changed from the top I believe the 88 should be the same.<BR>AC belt may have to be changed from the bottom.   <p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 03-25-2001).]||||reg||1
